From fc53f0aabe9d643b35279dd84f3d6d160f6e656a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koudai Aono <koxudaxi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:36:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] mellum: optimized q8 prefill and decode

Tiled expert GEMMs from 32 rows and batched Q8_0 projections, Metal 4
tensor-tile experts (E1), prefill attention tiles with half operands, and the
decode fusions (q/k norm and RoPE, K/V staged as f16, the MoE reduce with its
residual, and add plus RMS norm) in one dispatch each. The exact rows kernel
stays for chunks under 32 rows, and DS4_MELLUM_EXACT_PREFILL=1 keeps every
chunk exact for diagnostics.

The A/B/B/A CLI runners, their model-free contract and the 2048-token decode
prompt ship with the patch; the ported tests are test_mellum_fastpath.sh and
the exact-prefill and deep-rewind cases in ds4_test.

Also carried: the f32 tiled-attention experiment removed (0ea33285), the sliding decode kernel's two-key loads
(6604b190), and the sliding reference kernel with its comparison (f160af74). The shared Metal compile-options
helper from patches/common is restored after the reference's compiler setup replaced it.

Gates: test-mellum-kernels 662/662; test-mellum-fastpath 45/45; exact prefill differs from decode in 0 of
98,304 logit words under the diagnostic and 98,301 without; test-qwen4-kernels
passes; ds4_test --mellum-rewind (with the frontier k=1 case) OK. Same-machine
2.3 pair on this M5 Max, n=6: port 3,987 t/s prefill and 125.08 t/s decode
against the d2d9338 reference's 3,967 and 124.67.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: upstream has equivalent Mellum fast paths
